 "problems": [
  "Row has 12 numeric columns after Common Interest (two amounts each for 6 categories: Common Charges w/o Contribution, RE Taxes Year1, RE Taxes Year2, Carrying Costs w/o Contribution, Common Charges w/ Contribution monthly/annual) but only 5 labeled pairs fit the schema; I mapped: cc_m/cc_a = Est. Common Charges without Contribution, tax_m/tax_a = Est. Real Estate Taxes First Year, tax2_m = Est. Real Estate Taxes Second Year monthly, carry_m = Est. Carrying Costs monthly. The last pair (Est. Common Charges with Contribution monthly/annual) is not captured in any schema field and is omitted.",
  "Total row's cc_m (72048.58) taken as \"without Contribution\" monthly figure per column order; ext_sf total (1856 SF) is the Uninhabitable Ltd. Common Element total, not a separate outdoor space, and was excluded from TOTAL ext_sf per instructions (sf2, not ext_sf).",
  "Units with \"T\" or \"B\" Ltd. Common Element (terrace/balcony) have area given in the \"Uninhabitable Ltd. Common Element Approx. Area\" column, which per rules I placed in sf2 rather than ext_sf since the column header explicitly says \"Uninhabitable\" and the SF2 field was already used for that same column for non-terrace units (uninhabitable interior areas like storage). This is a judgment call - the T/B areas (e.g. 1A:122 T, 2E:80 B) may actually represent terrace/balcony ext_sf rather than uninhabitable interior space."
 ],
